=== SIGNATURE ===
set_d(a, b, [as_row])

=== COMMENT ===
Set difference: the values in set a that are not in set b.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(val_a, val_b, [as_row],
   LET(_r,
      LET(
         list_a, set(val_a),
         list_b, set(val_b),
         res, FILTER(list_a, ISNA(XMATCH(list_a, list_b))),
         IF(z_opt(0, as_row), TOROW(res), res)
      ),
      IF(ISERROR(_r), "", _r)
   )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Set difference of two ranges (a minus b).

Arguments:
  a        - first range/set.
  b        - second range/set.
  [as_row] - 1 for a horizontal result; default 0 vertical.

Single-value arguments (flags, counts, delimiters, a single lookup value) may arrive as 1x1 arrays (TOCOL(x), {x}, a one-cell FILTER/INDEX result); they are collapsed to true scalars with z_scalar, so they behave exactly like the plain value.

Optional arguments: a blank cell or "" behaves like omitting the argument (the default applies), and a number given as text ("2") is accepted as the number (z_opt).

Returns:
  The cleaned, sorted values that appear in a but not in b.

Example:
  set_d(A1:A5, B1:B5)
